**You're right, DIR and DMU are not the same, and my suggestion in Q6 was wrong for DMU.** I checked the screen code and the stored procedures.

| | DIR | DMU |
|---|---|---|
| Task's own "Bill No." field on the screen | Yes (`txtDelBillNo`, loaded only when the system code is DIR) | No |
| Bill No. per installment line (Prior Information) | Yes | Yes |
| Screen procedure returns `Tax_Info.BillNumber` | Yes | No |

So for DMU a processor can only enter a Bill Number on the installment lines, which are stored in `tbl_ExceptionQueue_Tax_YearInfo`. The `Tax_Info.BillNumber` column still exists for DMU, but the screen never shows it. The MPS inbound save does write to it, which is the likely source of the few DMU values in DEV (I did not trace them).

DEV data for the items currently staged to MPS:

| Staged items | DIR (8,737) | DMU (645) |
|---|---|---|
| Task-level Bill No. filled (`Tax_Info`) | 0 | 5 |
| Bill No. filled on the line for the item's own year and installment | 2 | 0 |
| Bill No. filled on any line | 3 | 8 |

**Revised suggestion:** use one rule for both types. Take the task-level Bill No. first; if it is empty, take the Bill No. from the line with the same tax year and installment as the payload item. That covers the DIR field and the DMU lines, and it is the same "first this, else that" pattern you already chose for Follow-up Date.

